# ============================================================================
# Databricks Module - Variables
# ============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
#   This file defines input variables for the Databricks module.
#   These are the parameters that must be provided when calling this module.
#   Unlike root module variables, module variables don't have defaults unless
#   explicitly defined here.
#
# KEY CONCEPTS FOR BEGINNERS:
#   - Module variables: Inputs that the calling module must provide
#   - Required vs optional: Variables without defaults are required
#   - Variable types: Same as root module variables (string, number, bool, etc.)
#   - Module inputs: Passed from root module using module block
#
# TERRAFORM DOCUMENTATION:
#   - Module Variables: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/develop/variables
#   - Module Inputs: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/syntax#calling-a-child-module
#
# USAGE EXAMPLE:
#   In the root module, you would call this module like:
#   module "databricks" {
#     source = "./modules/databricks"
#     workspace_name = "my-workspace"
#     # ... other variables
#   }
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED VARIABLES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Name of the Databricks workspace
# This will appear in the Databricks UI and URLs
# Example: "myproject-workspace"
variable "workspace_name" {
  description = "Name of the Databricks workspace (will appear in URLs and UI)"
  type        = string
  # No default - this must be provided by the calling module
}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: Additional Variables
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In a complete module implementation, you would also have variables for:
# - account_id: Databricks account ID
# - pricing_tier: STANDARD, PREMIUM, or ENTERPRISE
# - network_id: VPC/VNet network configuration
# - storage_configuration_id: Storage bucket configuration
# - credentials_id: IAM role/service principal credentials
# - region: Cloud provider region
# - tags: Resource tags
# - And other provider-specific configuration options
